  "solution": {
    "text": "Aniline is a primary amine (contains - $\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group). When it is treated with chloroform under alkaline conditions, it results in the formation of a bad smelling compound, known by the name isonitrile or carbylamine. This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction. <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a44.png\">",
